course: dictionary
lesson: 9035
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one you need. Slash can be an action word (a verb) or a naming word (a noun). «The forest is speckled and sprottled and spottled, dotted and splashed and slashed and hatched and cross-hatched with shadows.» The words around slashed are all about marks on the ground, so here it means marked with streaks, not cut with a sword.
explain: Look at the clues around the word. If the sentence is about a sword, a blade or a fight, slash means to cut with a long, quick stroke. If it is about prices in a shop, «prices slashed!» means the prices have been cut by a lot. If it is about numbers like 3/4, the slash is a symbol.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does "prices cut by a lot" make sense in the shop sentence? Yes, so you have the right meaning. If it does not fit, try another meaning from the list.
fact: Slash can be a verb (slash, slashes, slashed, slashing) or a noun (a slash, slashes).
fact: To slash means to cut with a long, quick, strong stroke of a blade.
fact: To slash prices means to reduce them by a lot, so shoppers pay less.
fact: A slash is also the sloping line / used in fractions like 3/4, in dates and in web addresses.
fact: Dates differ: in the UK 10/10/2026 means day/month/year, but in the USA it means month/day/year.
exercise: «Prices slashed!» says the shop window. What does slashed mean here? | *Reduced by a lot | Painted bright red | Lost on the way home | Cut with a sword in a fight
exercise: «The knight slashed at the dragon with his sword.» What does slashed mean? | Shouted loudly | *Cut with a long, quick stroke | Walked very slowly | Lit up brightly
exercise: In the fraction 3/4, what is the slash? | A word meaning cut | A kind of sword | *A sloping line used in fractions | A sign that the shop is closed
test: In the UK, the date 05/06/2026 means which day? | 26 May 2006 | 5 May 2026 | 6 May 2026 | *5 June 2026
test: «The painter made a long slash of red across the page.» Is slash a noun or a verb here? | Adjective, meaning very red | *Noun, meaning a long mark or cut | Adverb, meaning quickly | Verb, meaning to cut
exam: In «The forest is speckled and sprottled and spottled, dotted and splashed and slashed and hatched and cross-hatched with shadows», what does slashed most likely describe? | *Long streaks of shadow across the forest | A fraction in a sum | Prices cut in a shop | A sword fight between two knights
